\subsection{Interpretation and comparison limits}

Both OpenAI datasets use Qdrant DBpedia embeddings \cite{data_openai1536,data_openai3072}. After truncation/renormalisation, 1,000 query and 10,299 sampled base rows have cosine $\geq0.9980$ (median 1.000000), with GT overlap 9.046/10. Without entity IDs, these checks support row alignment. Doubling width leaves CAGRA ratios at 1.747 and RaBitQ at 1.130/1.157, so width alone is insufficient.

At 128 probes, larger gains accompany smaller refinement multipliers: OpenAI 4--8, Vogue 64, arXiv 100 (later FULL 200). This is an observed association; matched-recall comparisons may select other settings.

\Cref{sec:7-8} checks sensitivity to small margins and the interface/memory/compilation differences of \cref{sec:3-3}.


