\subsection{Shared bounds preserve the selection target}



All 48 outputs agree; QPS ratios span $0.994$--$1.562\times$. At arXiv $\alpha=200$, batch 1,000 and eight groups, sharing cuts merge 2,629$\to$471\,$\mu$s and scan 7,968$\to$5,513\,$\mu$s. Some cells regress slightly.

The pilot's first group holds 46--81\% of winners. Equal quotas need fallback; unequal ones retain a bottleneck. Bounds avoid fixed quotas.

